// The pattern engine, written in Cufet.
//
// This file is bundled into the checker (see TypeChecker.WithPrelude): every program is checked and
// compiled as though it began with these statements.
//
// ★★ It declares NO module, and that is the point. A book on a LANGUAGE offers no members — you
// pull it to write patterns at all, not to call things on it — so the engine must not become
// `regex's match`. Everything below is a top-level helper, and BookLoading.MakePrivate renames each
// one after the book it belongs to: `match` becomes `match in regex`, a name with a space in it,
// which no identifier may contain. Unwritable, uncollidable, and reached only by the code the
// parser lowers a pattern into.
//
// ⚠⚠ EVERY NAME THIS FILE BINDS IS PREFIXED `rx-`, and that is not decoration. These helpers are
// spliced into EVERY Cufet program, and a top-level function's local shares a scope with a
// program's shared constants — so an unprefixed `Define total` here made `Define total as 42
// permanently.` refuse to compile in any program on earth. MEASURED: it broke a documented sample
// in GRAMMAR.md, and the doc fence tests are what caught it.
//
// ★ That collision is a LANGUAGE bug and predates this file — a top-level `Bind` whose body
// declares a local, plus a later `permanently` constant of the same name, is refused with no
// prelude involved at all, and the message blames the function's local for a conflict the constant
// caused. The prefix is this file staying out of its way, not a fix for it. A module member does
// not have the problem, which is why `collections` never hit it.
//
// ★★ Written in Cufet because the ORACLE requires it, not as a preference. Two engines — .NET's
// Regex interpreted and POSIX regcomp compiled — would disagree about greediness, character
// classes and empty matches, silently, on inputs nobody thought to test. The prelude is spliced in
// before either backend sees a program, so there is exactly one of this and nothing to diverge.
//
// ★ An AUTOMATON, never backtracking. A backtracking engine can hang forever on a pattern that
// looks fine; the usual defence is a timeout, and a timeout is nondeterministic where the oracle
// demands byte-for-byte agreement. It matters more here than elsewhere: this engine is itself
// written in Cufet, so backtracking's worst case on a slow host is not "slow" but "never finishes".
//
// The compiled form is a series of records, built by RegexPattern.Compile:
//   kind 0 — match this character, then go to `step`
//   kind 1 — match any one character, then go to `step`
//   kind 2 — go to `step` or to `alt`, consuming nothing
//   kind 3 — accept
//   kind 4 — `^`: go to `step`, but only with nothing consumed yet
//   kind 5 — `$`: go to `step`, but only with everything consumed
//   kind 6 — `[^…]`: match any one character NOT in `ch`, then go to `step`
// `step` and `alt` are 1-based positions in the same series; 0 means nowhere. State 1 is the entry.
//
// ⚠ This list is the map a reader navigates by, and it described kinds 0-3 for an hour after 4 and
// 5 existed. Adding a kind means adding a line HERE, in RegexPattern's constants, and in `reach`.
//
// ⚠ The four field names are a contract with RegexPattern.State, and nothing checks that the two
// agree. A change on either side is a change on both.

/// Marks one state live, and follows every branch out of it that consumes nothing.
///
/// ⚠ The already-live check is what makes an epsilon CYCLE terminate — `(ab)*` reaches its own
/// branch again without consuming anything, and without this the walk would not stop.
///
/// ★★ `rx-seen` is how many characters of the subject have been consumed so far, and `rx-total` is
/// how many there are. They exist only for the ANCHORS: every other state is answerable from the
/// state series alone, which is why the engine needed nothing but the program until now. An anchor
/// consumes nothing, so it is followed here with the branches — but it is a gate rather than a
/// fork, and a path that reaches it in the wrong place simply stops.
Bind void to reach, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) rx-program,
    the number rx-index,
    the series of fact rx-active,
    the number rx-seen,
    the number rx-total):
    If rx-index is 0, return.
    If item rx-index of rx-active is true, return.
    The item rx-index of rx-active becomes true.
    Define rx-node as item rx-index of rx-program.
    If the kind of rx-node is 2:
        Cast reach on (rx-program, the step of rx-node, rx-active, rx-seen, rx-total).
        Cast reach on (rx-program, the alt of rx-node, rx-active, rx-seen, rx-total).
    Done.
    // `^` — only where nothing has been consumed yet.
    If the kind of rx-node is 4:
        If rx-seen is 0, cast reach on (rx-program, the step of rx-node, rx-active, rx-seen, rx-total).
    Done.
    // `$` — only where everything has.
    If the kind of rx-node is 5:
        If rx-seen is rx-total, cast reach on (rx-program, the step of rx-node, rx-active, rx-seen, rx-total).
    Done.
Done.

/// Is any accepting state live?
Bind fact to accepting, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) rx-program,
    the series of fact rx-active):
    Define rx-index as 0.
    For each rx-node in rx-program, repeat:
        Increment rx-index by 1.
        If item rx-index of rx-active is true:
            If the kind of rx-node is 3, return true.
        Done.
    Done.
    Return false.
Done.

/// A fresh all-false liveness map, one entry per state.
Bind series of fact to blank, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) rx-program):
    Define rx-flags as a series of fact.
    For each rx-node in rx-program, repeat:
        Insert false into rx-flags.
    Done.
    Return rx-flags.
Done.

/// Does the subject hold a match for this pattern anywhere in it?
///
/// ★ The set of live states is carried forward one character at a time, which is what makes the
/// cost linear in the subject however the pattern is shaped. `a*a*a*a*b` against a long run of a's
/// with no b — the input that makes a backtracking engine hang — is answered in one pass.
Bind fact to match, given (
    the series of records like (the number kind, the text ch, the number step, the number alt) rx-program,
    the text rx-subject):
    If the number of rx-program is 0, return false.

    Define rx-total as the length of rx-subject.

    Define rx-active as cast blank on (rx-program).
    Cast reach on (rx-program, 1, rx-active, 0, rx-total).
    // Before consuming anything: a pattern that can match nothing at all matches here. ★ This is
    // also where `[^$]` against an empty subject is answered — nothing consumed is also everything
    // consumed when there is nothing to consume, so both gates open.
    If cast accepting on (rx-program, rx-active), return true.

    For each rx-pos in range 1 to rx-total, repeat:
        Define rx-here as the characters from rx-pos to rx-pos of rx-subject.
        Define rx-onward as cast blank on (rx-program).
        Define rx-index as 0.
        For each rx-node in rx-program, repeat:
            Increment rx-index by 1.
            If item rx-index of rx-active is true:
                If the kind of rx-node is 0:
                    If the ch of rx-node is rx-here, cast reach on (rx-program, the step of rx-node, rx-onward, rx-pos, rx-total).
                Done.
                If the kind of rx-node is 1:
                    Cast reach on (rx-program, the step of rx-node, rx-onward, rx-pos, rx-total).
                Done.
                // `[^…]` — the ch holds every EXCLUDED character, so membership is the test and
                // failing it is what lets the path through. ★ `contains` is exact-substring, and
                // rx-here is exactly one character, so this is character membership.
                If the kind of rx-node is 6:
                    If the ch of rx-node contains rx-here is false:
                        Cast reach on (rx-program, the step of rx-node, rx-onward, rx-pos, rx-total).
                    Done.
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        // Unanchored: a match may begin at any position, so the entry state is always live. This is
        // what makes the answer "does the subject HOLD a match", which is what the first slice's
        // `contains` lowering meant — the two must keep agreeing.
        //
        // ★★ And this line is exactly where `^` earns its keep, without a single special case: the
        // entry is still re-seeded at every position, but a pattern beginning with a start anchor
        // now meets that gate with rx-pos characters already consumed, so every late start dies on
        // its own. Anchoring is the ABSENCE of a path, not the removal of this line.
        Cast reach on (rx-program, 1, rx-onward, rx-pos, rx-total).
        The rx-active becomes rx-onward.
        If cast accepting on (rx-program, rx-active), return true.
    Done.
    Return false.
Done.
